            members: {
                gurselGecir: { about: "Originally from Giresun, Gürsel is a 3rd-year Electrical and Electronics Engineering student at Sakarya University, a founding member of SEIS, and currently serves as the President of SEIS for the new term. In the previous term, he was responsible for member recruitment in the Human Resources Department, where he played a strategic role in managing the club’s internal dynamics and ensuring communication between departments. With his social personality and active lifestyle, Gürsel brings energy to his team and aims to lead SEIS in the new term and contribute to the club’s development with his passion for technology and management." },
                mehmetZahidGorgec: { about: "Born in Konya, Mehmet Zahid GÖRGEÇ is a 3rd-year Computer Engineering student. He continues to develop his interest in software on an academic basis, focusing on artificial intelligence and user-centered software development. He works in our team as a UI/UX & Digital Experience Specialist and aims to contribute to making digital platforms more understandable, accessible, and effective." },
                beratKaanAydin: { about: "Our Vice President is responsible for team discipline and internal relations. He manages communication between members and follows the implementation of the club’s internal rules. He adopts a fair and transparent management approach. He organizes social events to maintain and strengthen team spirit. With his solution-oriented approach, he helps ensure harmony and a positive environment within the team. Working alongside the President, he supports the club’s operations, contributes to stronger coordination between departments, and helps develop SEIS’s organizational structure." },
                ensarDavut: { about: "Ensar Davud is an Electrical and Electronics Engineering student at Sakarya University, the founder and first-term president of the Sakarya Engineering & Innovation Society (SEIS). He founded SEIS to create an environment where students can develop not only academically but also in terms of vision, leadership, and productivity. In the new term, he continues to oversee the club’s management processes, activities, and development as a member of the Supervisory Board. He aims to help preserve the founding vision and values of SEIS, while guiding the new management team with his experience and supporting the club’s sustainable development." },
                senanurBektas: { about: "Senanur Bektaş is a 2nd-year English Translation and Interpreting student at Sakarya University and serves as the Corporate Communication and External Relations Coordinator at SEIS. Combining her academic journey with intercultural communication studies, Bektaş also works part-time as a language instructor, strengthening her professional experience. Seeing communication not only as a way of sharing information but also as a process of creating shared value, Senanur manages the community’s external communication strategies and develops visionary projects." },
                zeynepCenik: { about: "Zeynep is a Chemistry student at Sakarya University and serves as the PR & Marketing Coordinator at SEIS. Seeing communication not only as a way to make announcements but also as a force that brings people together around a common purpose, Zeynep manages digital content creation, social media management, and event promotion processes. Her main goal is to increase SEIS’s visibility and build a sincere, sustainable, and strong communication network for the community." },
                nurcinVatansever: { about: "Nurçin is an Industrial Engineering student at Sakarya University and serves as the Department of Services and Event Coordinator at SEIS. She actively takes part in organization, teamwork, and communication processes, taking responsibility for the planning, coordination, and execution of events. She values building strong communication with people and bringing different ideas together around a common goal. By applying the analytical thinking and planning skills gained from her Industrial Engineering education to club activities, she aims to contribute to making SEIS a more active and effective community." },
                bilgehanYetkin: { about: "Responsible for SEIS’s resource development and fundraising processes. Plans sponsorship and donation processes to support the sustainability of the club, communicates with potential supporters, and develops partnerships. Ensures that financial resources are used efficiently and helps create new income opportunities. Aims to contribute to the club’s projects and events by developing creative fundraising ideas. With strong communication and persuasion skills, strengthens SEIS’s relationships with external partners and contributes to the club’s financial sustainability." }

            }
